## 3880b65 Say what a retired key serves: a live tunnel's heartbeat and its new connections, nothing else

README.md and relay.py's comments said that a retired hash in ping_keys serves only a heartbeat. Since batch 7's fix, link_refusal
also takes one on NewUserConn, for a tunnel already logged in, so that a key change leaves its new connections open (R6.1). Batch 7's
delta review, its Minor. An API call, a Login and a registration still need the current key, and the README now says so.

Proven by: test_r6_1_no_text_says_a_heartbeat_is_all_a_retired_key_serves failed on each of the five claims and on the missing line
before the text changed, and passes now. No behaviour changed.

